[SECURITY]
UID: SEC-TEMPLATE-THREAT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template hostile input across the safety boundary
TYPE: Threat
DESCRIPTION: An attacker or compromised lower-assurance component sends malformed, stale, replayed, reordered, unauthorized, or excessive-rate input across the safety boundary to alter behavior or prevent a required safety response.
LIFECYCLE_PHASES: Commissioning, operation, maintenance, update, and recovery
OPERATING_MODES: Remote, autonomous, degraded, service, recovery, and update
ASSETS: SEC-TEMPLATE-ASSET-001
TRUST_BOUNDARY: The threat crosses DES-TEMPLATE-IF-001 from the lower-assurance communications domain into the safety controller.
ATTACK_SURFACE: Network protocol, message parser, command interface, status interface, diagnostic interface, resource queues, and recovery path
THREAT_ACTORS: >>>
- remote unauthenticated attacker
- authenticated but unauthorized user
- compromised operator or maintenance account
- compromised communications component
- malicious or compromised supplier component
- person with local physical or diagnostic access.
<<<
ATTACK_PATH: >>>
1. Obtain access to an exposed communications or maintenance path.
2. Construct input that violates identity, authorization, schema, range,
   freshness, sequence, state, or rate expectations.
3. Send the input across the safety boundary.
4. Attempt to influence safety logic, exhaust resources, suppress diagnostics,
   alter protected state, or delay the safe response.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: The attack may delay or inhibit a protective stop, alter protected configuration, trigger hazardous motion, cause denial of service, conceal a fault, or invalidate retained evidence.
RISK_METHOD: Replace with the approved security risk method and revision
INITIAL_RISK: Replace with likelihood, attacker capability, exposure, consequence, safety impact, uncertainty, and resulting initial risk
SAFETY_IMPACT: The threat can contribute to SAFE-TEMPLATE-HAZ-001 by interfering with SAFE-TEMPLATE-FUNC-001.
RESIDUAL_RISK: Not yet evaluated
ACCEPTANCE_RATIONALE: Further risk reduction is required through least privilege, authentication, authorization, input validation, replay protection, rate limiting, resource partitioning, monitoring, safe fallback, and independent safety behavior.
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Interface robustness testing, abuse-case testing, fuzzing, resource-exhaustion testing, fault injection, penetration testing, and safety-response verification
OWNER: Template threat owner
REVIEWER: Replace with competent security and safety reviewers
REVIEW_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
TAGS: template, security, threat, safety-boundary
