[SECURITY]
UID: SEC-TEMPLATE-CTRL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template defensive safety-boundary control
TYPE: SecurityControl
DESCRIPTION: Treat all lower-assurance input as untrusted and enforce authentication, authorization, validation, freshness, sequencing, rate limits, resource limits, deterministic arbitration, diagnostics, and safe fallback at the safety boundary.
LIFECYCLE_PHASES: Commissioning, operation, maintenance, update, recovery, and decommissioning
OPERATING_MODES: All modes permitting communication across the safety boundary
ASSETS: SEC-TEMPLATE-ASSET-001
TRUST_BOUNDARY: DES-TEMPLATE-IF-001
ATTACK_SURFACE: Operational messages, privileged commands, diagnostics, update coordination, reset requests, recovery requests, and status responses
CONSEQUENCES: Failure of the control can transfer unauthorized authority into the safety boundary or allow lower-assurance behavior to interfere with a required safety response.
CONTROL_TYPE: Preventive
SECURITY_OBJECTIVES: >>>
- authenticate privileged sources
- authorize commands according to identity, state, and role
- validate schema, type, range, length, state, and integrity
- reject stale, replayed, duplicated, reordered, and excessive-rate traffic
- constrain CPU, memory, storage, queue, network, and logging consumption
- prioritize safety behavior over operational requests
- preserve safe fallback during communication failure or attack
- retain security-relevant rejection and diagnostic evidence
- prevent external input from clearing a latched safety condition.
<<<
SAFETY_IMPACT: The control protects REQ-TEMPLATE-SAFE-001, SAFE-TEMPLATE-FUNC-001, and the assumptions of DES-TEMPLATE-ARCH-001.
RESIDUAL_RISK: Replace after implementation, security verification, safety verification, and representative validation
ACCEPTANCE_RATIONALE: The control is accepted only when hostile and malformed input cannot prevent the required safe response within its allocated timing and resource limits.
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Code review, static analysis, protocol conformance, fuzzing, abuse-case testing, penetration testing, resource testing, fault injection, timing measurement, and regression testing
EVIDENCE: Replace with controlled design, implementation, security-test, fault-injection, timing, and review evidence
OWNER: Template security-control owner
REVIEWER: Replace with an independent security reviewer and required safety reviewer
REVIEW_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
TAGS: template, security, control, safety-boundary
