[SECURITY]
UID: SEC-TEMPLATE-VULN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template vulnerability-management process
TYPE: VulnerabilityManagement
DESCRIPTION: Establish a controlled process to receive, assess, prioritize, remediate, verify, disclose, and monitor vulnerabilities affecting released and supported product configurations.
LIFECYCLE_PHASES: Development, production, operation, maintenance, update, end of support, and decommissioning
ASSETS: Product software, firmware, hardware, dependencies, build systems, deployment infrastructure, credentials, safety assumptions, and retained evidence
TRUST_BOUNDARY: Product, supplier, development, build, update, support, and field-service boundaries
ATTACK_SURFACE: Public reports, supplier advisories, dependency inventories, scanners, testing, incident reports, and field telemetry
THREAT_ACTORS: Researchers, customers, suppliers, opportunistic attackers, targeted attackers, insiders, and automated scanning systems
CONSEQUENCES: Unmanaged vulnerabilities can remain exploitable, invalidate security or safety assumptions, prevent timely remediation, and expose unsupported products to unacceptable risk.
CONTROL_TYPE: Responsive
SECURITY_OBJECTIVES: >>>
- maintain an accurate component and dependency inventory
- provide a documented vulnerability-reporting channel
- assess exploitability, exposure, consequence, and safety impact
- assign ownership and response timelines
- develop and review mitigations or updates
- verify remediation and required regression
- notify affected stakeholders
- preserve decisions, evidence, and residual-risk acceptance
- define support periods and end-of-support behavior.
<<<
SAFETY_IMPACT: Every vulnerability assessment must determine whether the issue can create a hazard, inhibit a risk control, affect a safety function, or invalidate safety evidence.
RESIDUAL_RISK: Replace with the accepted risk for unresolved or deferred vulnerabilities
ACCEPTANCE_RATIONALE: Vulnerabilities are accepted only by authorized roles using the approved risk method and with documented compensating controls, affected configurations, expiry conditions, and monitoring.
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Process audit, dependency and component review, remediation testing, regression testing, update validation, and closure review
EVIDENCE: Replace with vulnerability records, assessments, remediation commits, test reports, advisories, decisions, and closure evidence
OWNER: Template product security response owner
REVIEWER: Replace with competent security, product, and safety reviewers as applicable
REVIEW_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
TAGS: template, security, vulnerability-management, field-monitoring
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEC-TEMPLATE-CTX-001
  ROLE: Derived from
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEC-TEMPLATE-ASSET-001
