[SECURITY]
UID: SEC-TEMPLATE-INC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template security incident response
TYPE: IncidentResponse
DESCRIPTION: Establish a controlled process to detect, triage, contain, investigate, recover from, communicate, and learn from security incidents affecting product or safety behavior.
LIFECYCLE_PHASES: Production, deployment, operation, maintenance, update, recovery, end of support, and decommissioning
OPERATING_MODES: All operational, service, recovery, and update modes
ASSETS: Product availability, safety behavior, credentials, protected data, configuration, logs, evidence, customer trust, and regulatory obligations
TRUST_BOUNDARY: Product, operational, support, supplier, cloud, update, and safety boundaries
ATTACK_SURFACE: Monitoring alerts, field reports, anomalous behavior, authentication events, update failures, safety events, and vulnerability disclosures
THREAT_ACTORS: External attackers, insiders, compromised suppliers, compromised customers, malicious applications, and unknown actors
CONSEQUENCES: An ineffective response can prolong unsafe or insecure exposure, destroy evidence, spread compromise, cause incorrect recovery, or leave fielded products in an unknown configuration.
CONTROL_TYPE: Recovery
SECURITY_OBJECTIVES: >>>
- define incident severity and escalation criteria
- preserve logs and forensic evidence
- identify affected products and immutable baselines
- assess immediate and potential safety impact
- contain compromise without defeating required safety behavior
- revoke or rotate compromised credentials
- restore an approved configuration
- verify recovery and required regression
- communicate with customers, suppliers, authorities, and assessors
- feed lessons into threats, controls, requirements, tests, and field monitoring.
<<<
SAFETY_IMPACT: Incidents with potential safety impact require immediate coordination with the safety authority and reassessment of affected hazards, controls, functions, evidence, and release decisions.
RESIDUAL_RISK: Replace with the accepted post-incident risk and follow-up actions
ACCEPTANCE_RATIONALE: Incident closure requires identified affected configurations, contained exposure, approved recovery, verified corrective actions, preserved evidence, and authorized residual-risk acceptance.
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Tabletop exercises, recovery drills, communication exercises, evidence-retention checks, credential-rotation tests, and post-incident review
EVIDENCE: Replace with exercise reports, incident records, timelines, forensic evidence, recovery verification, communications, and corrective-action closure
OWNER: Template incident-response owner
REVIEWER: Replace with competent security, operations, legal, compliance, and safety reviewers as applicable
REVIEW_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
TAGS: template, security, incident-response, recovery
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEC-TEMPLATE-CTX-001
  ROLE: Derived from
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEC-TEMPLATE-VULN-001
  ROLE: Derived from

